      abbreviations: ["CBF", "CPP", "MAP", "ICP"],
      definition: "Cerebral blood flow is delivery of oxygen- and glucose-carrying blood to brain tissue. Cerebral autoregulation is the arteriolar response that normally keeps that flow relatively stable as perfusion pressure changes. Cerebral perfusion pressure, commonly framed as mean arterial pressure (MAP) minus intracranial pressure, describes the pressure gradient pushing blood through the brain. These ideas matter in stroke because a blocked artery removes normal inflow, while hypotension, hypoxemia, edema, fever, or rising intracranial pressure can further starve tissue that is already surviving on collateral circulation.",
